From: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
Subject: [PATCH] nss_shaper: drain the interface bounce callback on unregister

nss_shaper_unregister_shaper_bounce_bridge() waits for reg->callback_active
to clear before it drops the registration and calls module_put(); the
interface sibling twenty lines above it does not. Both are torn down the
same way and both are called from a module that the bounce callback runs
in, so the asymmetry is the bug: a bounce callback already dispatched by
nss_shaper_bounced_callback() can still be running inside the registrant
when module_put() releases the last reference to the module holding it.

Add the same wait to the interface path, byte for byte the sibling's.

The trigger is root removing a bounce qdisc, so this is well below the
bar the rest of the audit applied and the reason it was left alone. What
makes it worth the five lines is that the correct sequence is already
present in the same file, so this is restoring an invariant rather than
inventing one.

Signed-off-by: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>

--- a/nss_shaper.c
+++ b/nss_shaper.c
@@ -123,6 +123,15 @@ void nss_shaper_unregister_shaper_bounce
 	}
 
 	/*
+	 * Wait until any bounce callback that is active is finished
+	 */
+	while (reg->callback_active) {
+		spin_unlock_bh(&nss_top->lock);
+		yield();
+		spin_lock_bh(&nss_top->lock);
+	}
+
+	/*
 	 * Unegister
 	 */
 	owner = reg->owner;
